2. kui_toy_movie_ahead_update with toy_wire_update_seen inlined. It runs on the game's stack, outside the gate:
   28 bytes pushed. Every access to the game's memory is a read: the player's counters at ctx+0xac and ctx+0x90,
   its lag counter at 0x8c1138c4, and its buffer behind three pointers each checked by toy_chunk_ram. Every
   write goes to the reader's own kept block (R8). The gate is entered by a tail jump only when the call is
   passed on.

